hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15621","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Abu Said, meaning the teacher Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Abi al-Waddah, narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid and al-Mujalid ibn Said narrated to us, from Amir al-Shabi, from Amir ibn Shahr, he said: I heard two sayings, one saying from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and another from al-Najashi. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Look to Quraysh, take from their speech and leave their action. And I was sitting with al-Najashi, and his son came from school and recited a verse from the Gospel, and I recognized it or understood it, so I laughed. He said: What do you laugh at, at the Book of Allah Almighty. By Allah, indeed among what Allah Almighty revealed to Isa son of Maryam is that curse will be on earth when its rulers are children."
